/F2 9.5 Tf
(>> 5.1 Operational Amplifier Architecture and Ideal Characteristics) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(An Operational Amplifier \(Op-Amp\) is a high-gain DC-coupled differential voltage) Tj
T*
(amplifier designed to perform mathematical operations \(addition, subtraction,) Tj
T*
(integration, differentiation\) using negative feedback.) Tj
T*
(* Op-Amp Terminals: Non-inverting input \(+\), Inverting input \(-\), Output \(V_out\), and) Tj
T*
(DC power rails \(+V_CC, -V_EE\).) Tj
T*
(* Ideal Op-Amp Parameters \(Benchmark Comparison\):) Tj
T*
(1. Differential Voltage Gain A_vd = infinity \(Practically ~ 10^5 to 10^6\).) Tj
T*
(2. Input Impedance R_in = infinity \(Practically ~ 10^6 to 10^12 Omega, zero input) Tj
T*
(current: I+ = I- = 0\).) Tj
T*
(3. Output Impedance R_out = 0 \(Practically ~ 50 - 100 Omega\).) Tj
T*
(4. Bandwidth BW = infinity \(Can amplify signals from DC up to gigahertz\).) Tj
T*
(5. Common Mode Rejection Ratio \(CMRR\) = infinity \(Rejects all common-mode electrical) Tj
T*
(noise\).) Tj
T*
(6. Slew Rate SR = infinity \(Instantaneous output voltage change: dV_out/dt\).) Tj
T*
(7. Input Offset Voltage V_os = 0 \(V_out = 0 when V+ = V-\).) Tj
T*
(* Concept of Virtual Ground: When negative feedback is applied, infinite open-loop) Tj
T*
(gain forces the differential input voltage to zero: V_d = V+ - V- = V_out / A_vd =) Tj
T*
(V_out / infinity = 0. Therefore, V- = V+. If the non-inverting terminal is connected) Tj
T*
(to physical ground \(V+ = 0V\), the inverting terminal is held at virtual ground) Tj
T*
(potential \(V- = 0V\) without a direct physical ground connection.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
/F2 9.5 Tf
(>> 5.2 Linear Op-Amp Configurations) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(* Inverting Amplifier: Input applied to inverting terminal through resistor R1,) Tj
T*
(feedback resistor Rf connects output to inverting terminal; V+ = 0. By KCL at virtual) Tj
T*
(ground: I_in = I_f => \(V_in - 0\)/R1 = \(0 - V_out\)/Rf => Closed-Loop Gain A_v = V_out) Tj
T*
(/ V_in = - Rf / R1. Phase shift is 180 degrees.) Tj
T*
(* Non-Inverting Amplifier: Input applied directly to non-inverting terminal \(V+ =) Tj
T*
(V_in\). Voltage divider formed by R1 and Rf feeds back to inverting terminal: V- =) Tj
T*
(V_out * [ R1 / \(R1 + Rf\) ]. Setting V- = V+: V_out = V_in * [ 1 + Rf / R1 ]. Phase) Tj
T*
(shift is 0 degrees.) Tj
T*
(* Voltage Follower \(Buffer\): Non-inverting amplifier with Rf = 0 and R1 = infinity:) Tj
T*
(A_v = +1. Features ultra-high input impedance and very low output impedance,) Tj
T*
(isolating delicate biosensors from low-impedance recording loads.) Tj
T*
(* Summing Amplifier \(Adder\): Multiple inputs V1, V2, V3 connected through input) Tj
T*
(resistors to inverting node: V_out = - [ \(Rf/R1\)*V1 + \(Rf/R2\)*V2 + \(Rf/R3\)*V3 ].) Tj
T*
(* Difference Amplifier \(Subtractor\): V_out = \(Rf / R1\) * \(V2 - V1\), provided resistor) Tj
T*
(matching R3/R2 = Rf/R1 is satisfied.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
