(>> 5.3 Active Wave-Shaping: Integrators and Differentiators) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(* Op-Amp Integrator: Feedback resistor is replaced by a capacitor C. By KCL at) Tj
T*
(virtual ground: I_R = I_C => V_in / R = - C * \(dV_out / dt\).) Tj
T*
(V_out\(t\) = - \(1 / \(R * C\)\) * int_0^t V_in\(tau\) d\(tau\) + V_{initial}.) Tj
T*
(Converts square waves to triangular waves; acts as an active low-pass filter.) Tj
T*
(* Op-Amp Differentiator: Input element is capacitor C, feedback element is resistor) Tj
T*
(R: I_C = I_R => C * \(dV_in / dt\) = - V_out / R.) Tj
T*
(V_out\(t\) = - R * C * \(dV_in / dt\).) Tj
T*
(Converts triangular waves to square spikes; prone to high-frequency noise amplification.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
