([SOLVED PROBLEM 1: Inverting and Non-Inverting Amplifier Design]) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
/F2 9.5 Tf
(-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Problem: Design an inverting amplifier with a voltage gain of A_v = -12 and an input) Tj
T*
(impedance of 10 kOmega. If the op-amp is powered by +/- 15V rails and an input of V_in =) Tj
T*
(1.0 V is applied, calculate: \(1\) Values of R1 and Rf, \(2\) Output voltage V_out, \(3\)) Tj
T*
(Output voltage if V_in = 1.5 V.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 1: Component Values:) Tj
T*
(Input impedance of an inverting amplifier equals R1. Therefore: R1 = 10 kOmega.) Tj
T*
(Gain magnitude |A_v| = Rf / R1 = 12 => Rf = 12 * R1 = 12 * 10 kOmega = 120 kOmega.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 2: Output Voltage for V_in = 1.0 V:) Tj
T*
(V_out = A_v * V_in = \(-12\) * \(1.0 V\) = -12.0 Volts.) Tj
T*
(Since -12V is within the linear range \(-15V to +15V, accounting for saturation limit ~) Tj
T*
(+/-13.5V\), output is undistorted.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 3: Output Voltage for V_in = 1.5 V:) Tj
T*
(Theoretical V_out = \(-12\) * \(1.5 V\) = -18.0 Volts.) Tj
T*
(Saturation Check: The output cannot exceed the negative supply rail \(-15V\). The op-amp) Tj
T*
(enters negative saturation.) Tj
T*
(Actual Output: V_out ~ -13.5 V to -14.0 V \(Clipped at negative saturation\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
/F2 9.5 Tf
(-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
/F2 9.5 Tf
([SOLVED PROBLEM 2: Precision Summing Amplifier Calculation]) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
/F2 9.5 Tf
(-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Problem: An inverting summing amplifier has Rf = 100 kOmega, with three input resistors) Tj
T*
(R1 = 20 kOmega, R2 = 50 kOmega, and R3 = 10 kOmega connected to voltages V1 = +0.5 V, V2) Tj
T*
(= -1.0 V, and V3 = +0.2 V. Determine the output voltage V_out.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 1: Formula for Summing Amplifier:) Tj
T*
(V_out = - [ \(Rf / R1\) * V1 + \(Rf / R2\) * V2 + \(Rf / R3\) * V3 ].) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 2: Compute individual gain weighting factors:) Tj
T*
(Gain 1: Rf / R1 = 100 kOmega / 20 kOmega = 5.0.) Tj
T*
(Gain 2: Rf / R2 = 100 kOmega / 50 kOmega = 2.0.) Tj
T*
(Gain 3: Rf / R3 = 100 kOmega / 10 kOmega = 10.0.) Tj
T*
