T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Problem: An ideal Op-Amp integrator has R = 100 kOmega and C = 0.1 microF. A constant DC) Tj
T*
(step voltage of V_in = +2.0 V is applied at t = 0 with initial capacitor voltage V_c\(0\)) Tj
T*
(= 0. Determine: \(1\) Integrator time constant tau, \(2\) Rate of change of output voltage,) Tj
T*
(\(3\) Time required for the output to saturate at -13V.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 1: Compute Time Constant tau:) Tj
T*
(tau = R * C = \(100 * 10^3 Omega\) * \(0.1 * 10^-6 F\) = 0.01 seconds = 10 milliseconds.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 2: Rate of Change of Output Voltage dV_out/dt:) Tj
T*
(dV_out / dt = - V_in / \(R * C\) = - 2.0 V / 0.01 s = -200 Volts/second.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 3: Output Voltage Function:) Tj
T*
(V_out\(t\) = - 200 * t Volts \(a downward linear ramp\).) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 4: Time to Reach Saturation at V_out = -13 V:) Tj
T*
(-13 = - 200 * t => t_sat = 13 / 200 = 0.065 seconds = 65 milliseconds.) Tj
T*
(Conclusion: Output decreases linearly at 200 V/s until clipping at negative saturation) Tj
T*
(at t = 65 ms.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
/F2 9.5 Tf
(-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
/F2 9.5 Tf
([SOLVED PROBLEM 4: Instrumentation Difference Amplifier Analysis]) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
/F2 9.5 Tf
(-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Problem: In a bio-potential differential amplifier circuit, R1 = R2 = 10 kOmega, and) Tj
T*
(feedback resistors Rf = R4 = 100 kOmega. Common mode voltage V_cm = 5.0 V with a) Tj
T*
(biological differential ECG signal V_d = 20 mV \(V1 = 5.010 V, V2 = 4.990 V\). Verify that) Tj
T*
(the common mode voltage is rejected and calculate V_out.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 1: Verify Balanced Resistor Condition for Ideal CMRR:) Tj
T*
(Condition: R4 / R2 = Rf / R1 => 100k / 10k = 100k / 10k = 10.0 \(Condition strictly) Tj
T*
(satisfied\).) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 2: Calculate Output Voltage:) Tj
T*
(V_out = \(Rf / R1\) * \(V1 - V2\) = 10.0 * \(5.010 V - 4.990 V\) = 10.0 * \(0.020 V\) = 0.200) Tj
T*
(Volts = 200 mV.) Tj
T*
(Common Mode Rejection Check: The 5V DC common-mode bias is completely eliminated; only) Tj
T*
(the 20 mV ECG biopotential is amplified 10-fold to 200 mV.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
